The key rule: don't assert `result.is_err()`. That passes just as happily for the wrong error as for the right one, so it silently stops catching regressions. Assert the exact variant.

If `OrderError` implements `PartialEq`, `assert_eq!` above is enough. If it doesn't, match on the variant:

```rust
